A historical second-card carousel patch from Phase 5.

Do not apply this patch to the current repository: Voting now supplies the
second installed card naturally. It is retained only with the historical
design-fidelity evidence it produced. At the time, the Registry shipped one
game, so `browsingGameIndex` had nothing to move between and the Card Transition
— the 250ms ease-out §6 asked for — had nothing to animate on a shipped build.
This patch temporarily installed a second Trivia entry so the transition could
be driven and watched.

Both lists have to grow, and the server's is the one that is easy to forget:
`browseGame` clamps the index against `GAME_LOGIC_REGISTRY` in the Convex
deployment, so a patched client alone leaves the index pinned at 0 and the
television perfectly still.

It was a patch and not a fixture because a second game is a Registry decision
(`docs/CONTEXT.md`), and a hub that ships a fake one to make its animations
visible is a hub lying about what it installs.

diff --git a/packages/game-registry/src/logic.ts b/packages/game-registry/src/logic.ts
index ef56b86..dd9051f 100644
--- a/packages/game-registry/src/logic.ts
+++ b/packages/game-registry/src/logic.ts
@@ -12,7 +12,12 @@ import { clampBrowsingIndex } from './browsing';
  * Convex mutations that seed and reduce a game's state reach for this one, and
  * a module's screens are React Native that has no business in a server bundle.
  */
-export const GAME_LOGIC_REGISTRY: GameLogicRegistry = [triviaGameLogic];
+const secondCardLogic = {
+  ...triviaGameLogic,
+  metadata: { ...triviaGameLogic.metadata, id: 'second-card', title: 'SECOND CARD' },
+} as unknown as GameLogicRegistry[number];
+
+export const GAME_LOGIC_REGISTRY: GameLogicRegistry = [triviaGameLogic, secondCardLogic];
 
 /**
  * The installed game answering to `gameId`, or `undefined` if none does.
diff --git a/packages/game-registry/src/registry.ts b/packages/game-registry/src/registry.ts
